    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0314" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p1/pg270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/2–1952: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Portugal
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d144-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1952-02-19T18:00:00-05:00">February 19,
                            1952—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>436. For Dorsz. Emb Athens urges SEC and Mr. Lovett as well as Gen Bradley
                    indicate to Grk Reps at Lisbon our displeasure and anxiety at polit intervention
                        GAF.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d144-f2"/> Dept believes, if opportunity offers,
                    that emphasizing our views at that level might have salutary effect. Sakellariou
                    who is prime mover in “purge” of GAF, will be member of Grk Del.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d144-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d144-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was drafted by Porter (GTI) and signed for the Acting Secretary by
                    Rountree.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f2" n="2" xml:id="d144-f2-content">
                <p>This sentence is a paraphrase of telegram 3792, Feb. 19, from Athens, not
                    printed. (740.5/2–1952)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
